            <ArticleTitle>Chebyshev type inequalities by means of copulas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>272</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13660-017-1549-y</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A copula is a function which joins (or 'couples') a bivariate distribution function to its marginal (one-dimensional) distribution functions. In this paper, we obtain Chebyshev type inequalities by utilising copulas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
